/td></tr><tr><td align="left">Spectrin, beta, non-erythrocytic 1</td><td align="left">SPTBN1</td><td align="center">2.4E-05</td><td align="center">y</td><td align="center">y</td><td align="center">y</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left">Spectrin, alpha, non-erythrocytic 1</td><td align="left">SPTAN1</td><td align="center">3.5E-05</td><td align="center">y</td><td align="center">y</td><td></td><td align="center">y</td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left">Soc-2 suppressor of clear (<italic>C. elegans</italic>)</td><td align="left">SHOC2</td><td align="center">4.0E-05</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td align="center">y</td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left">Protein tyr. Phosph., receptor type, N 2</td><td align="left">PTPRN2</td><td align="center">4.6E-05</td><td align="center">y</td><td></td><td></td><td align="center">y</td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left">Potassium channel, subfamily K, member 3</td><td align="left">KCNK3</td><td align="center">4.7E-05</td><td align="center">y</td><td align="center">y</td><td align="center">y</td><td align="center">y</td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left">Neurotransmitter transporter, noradrenalin, member 2</td><td align="left">SLC6A2</td><td align="center">4.9E-05</td><td align="center">y</td><td align="center">y</td><td align="center">y</td><td align="center">y</td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left">Protein tyrosine phosphatase, non-receptor type 4</td><td align="left">PTPN4</td><td align="center">6.9E-05</td><td align="center">y</td><td></td><td></td><td align="center">y</td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left">Ras association (RalGDS/AF-6) domain family 1</td><td align="left">RASSF1</td><td align="center">7.6E-05</td><td align="center">y</td><td></td><td align="center">y</td><td align="center">y</td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left">Troponin T2, cardiac</td><td align="left">TNNT2</td><td align="center">7.9E-05</td><td></td><td align="center">y</td><td align="center">y</td><td></td><td align="center">y</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Inositol 1,4,5-trisphosphate 3-kinase B</td><td align="left">ITPKB</td><td align="center">8.7E-05</td><td align="center">y</td><td></td><td></td><td align="center">y</td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left">Ubiquitin specific protease 11</td><td align="left">USP11</td><td align="center">9.1E-05</td><td align="center">y</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left">Titin</td><td align="left">TTN</td><td align="center">1.0E-04</td><td></td><td align="center">y</td><td></td><td></td><td align="center">y</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><p><sup>a</sup>The HUGO name for the gene. Genes in the original query set are italicized.</p><p><sup>b</sup>MSGR combined <italic>P </italic>value. This <italic>P </italic>value was not adjusted to reflect multiple testing; a Bonferroni correction could be applied by multiplying each by 11 to account for searches at each node in the PMT.</p><p><sup>c</sup>Involved in cell &#x02013; cell or intracellular signaling.</p><p><sup>d</sup>Neuromuscular function.</p><p><sup>e</sup>Predicted binding site for the ZIC family of transcription factors.</p><p><sup>f</sup>Predicted binding site for MAZ or MAZR.</p><p><sup>g</sup>Predicted binding site for the BRAIN2 transcription factor.</p><p><sup>h</sup>A "y" indicates that a gene had a positive hit for a particular field.</p></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap position="float" id="T2"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p>Search result ranks for the <italic>Collagens </italic>pathway returned by the MSGR</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><td align="left"><bold>Query Gene</bold></td><td align="center"><bold>Human</bold></td><td align="center"><bold>Fly</bold></td><td align="center"><bold>Worm</bold></td><td align="center"><bold>Animal</bold></td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left">Collagen, type IV, alpha 2</td><td align="center">15</td><td align="center">98</td><td align="center">1</td><td align="center">1</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Nidogen 1</td><td align="center">189</td><td align="center">10</td><td align="center">146</td><td align="center">2</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Heparan sulfate proteoglycan 2</td><td align="center">5994</td><td align="center">52</td><td align="center">2</td><td align="center">4</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Collagen, type IV, alpha 5</td><td align="center">1218</td><td align="center">1</td><td align="center">n/a</td><td align="center">9</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Secreted protein, acidic, cysteine-rich</td><td align="center">20</td><td align="center">n/a*</td><td align="center">24</td><td align="center">6</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Laminin, beta 1</td><td align="center">1588</td><td align="center">34</td><td align="center">131</td><td align="center">8</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Laminin, alpha 2</td><td align="center">16</td><td align="center">158</td><td align="center">1728</td><td align="center">7</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Collagen, type XV, alpha 1</td><td align="center">12</td><td align="center">2291</td><td align="center">1193</td><td align="center">17</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Laminin, gamma 1</td><td align="center">10883</td><td align="center">23</td><td align="center">96</td><td align="center">12</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Lumican</td><td align="center">6</td><td align="center">1049</td><td align="center">n/a</td><td align="center">29</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Dystonin</td><td align="center">274</td><td align="center">103</td><td align="center">n/a</td><td align="center">50</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Collagen, type V, alpha 1</td><td align="center">87</td><td align="center">n/a</td><td align="center">5551</td><td align="center">263</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><p>*n/a corresponds to cases where no best target protein could be identified in a particular organism.</p></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap position="float" id="T3"><label>Table 3</label><caption><p>Top 25 genes returned by the Animal PMT node using the GenMAPP <italic>Collagens </italic>pathway as a query. The horizontal line indicates the 50% recall point, above which half of the query genes are included.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><td align="left"><bold>Gene Product<sup>a</sup></bold></td><td align="left">Symbol</td><td align="center"><italic>P</italic>-value<sup>b</sup></td><td align="center">A<sup>c</sup></td><td align="center">E<sup>d</sup></td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left"><italic>Collagen, type IV, alpha 2</italic></td><td align="left">COL4A2</td><td align="center">1.25E-09</td><td align="center">y<sup>e</sup></td><td align="center">y</td></tr><tr><td align="left"><italic>Nidogen</italic></td><td align="left">NID</td><td align="center">1.42E-07</td><td align="center">y</td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left">Actin binding LIM protein 1</td><td align="left">ABLIM1</td><td align="center">1.49E-07</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left"><italic>Heparan sulfate proteoglycan 2</italic></td><td align="left">HSPG2</td><td align="center">5.65E-07</td><td align="center">y</td><td align="center">y</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Spectrin, alpha, non-erythrocytic 1</td><td align="left">SPTAN1</td><td align="center">7.97E-07</td><td></td><td align="center">y</td></tr><tr><td align="left"><italic>Osteonectin</italic></td><td align="left">SPARC</td><td align="center">1.16E-06</td><td align="center">y</td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left"><italic>Laminin, alpha 2</italic></td><td align="left">LAMA2</td><td align="center">3.61E-06</td><td align="center">y</td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left"><italic>Laminin, beta 1</italic></td><td align="left">LAMB1</td><td align="center">4.89E-06</td><td align="center">y</td><td align="center">y</td></tr><tr><td colspan="5"><hr></hr></td></tr><tr><td align="left"><italic>Collagen, type IV, alpha 5 (Alport Syndrome)</italic></td><td align="left">COL4A5</td><td align="center">8.22E-06</td><td align="center">y</td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left">Ataxin 2</td><td align="left">ATXN2</td><td align="center">1.01E-05</td><td></td><td align="center">y</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Adipocyte, C1Q and collagen domain Containing</td><td align="left">ACDC</td><td align="center">1.44E-05</td><td></td><td align="center">n/a*</td></tr><tr><td align="left"><italic>Laminin, gamma 1 (formerly LAMB2)</italic></td><td align="left">LAMC1</td><td align="center">1.77E-05</td><td align="center">y</td><td align="center">y</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Syntaxin binding protein 1</td><td align="left">STXBP1</td><td align="center">1.95E-05</td><td></td><td align="center">y</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Calumenin</td><td align="left">CALU</td><td align="center">2.24E-05</td><td></td><td align="center">y</td></tr><tr><td align="left">High density lipoprotein binding protein (vigilin)</td><td align="left">HDLBP</td><td align="center">2.33E-05</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left">Crystallin, alpha B</td><td align="left">CRYAB</td><td align="center">2.41E-05</td><td></td><td align="center">y</td></tr><tr><td align="left"><italic>Collagen, type XV, alpha 1</italic></td><td align="left">COL15A1</td><td align="center">2.53E-05</td><td align="center">y</td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left">ATPase, H+ transporting, lysosomal accessory protein 1</td><td align="left">ATP6AP1</td><td align="center">2.57E-05</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left">Procollagen-lysine, 2-oxoglutarate 5- dioxygenase 3</td><td align="left">PLOD3</td><td align="center">2.89E-05</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left">Contactin 1</td><td align="left">CNTN1</td><td align="center">2.92E-05</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left">AMP-activated protein kinase family member 5</td><td align="left">ARK5</td><td align="center">2.93E-05</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td align="left">Integrin, alpha 8</td><td align="left">ITGA8</td><td align="center">3.13E-05</td><td></td><td align="center">n/a</td></tr><tr><td align="le